analysis relies on usage data; we do not read conversations as a routine practice; data is used to improve the Service and for AI research and development; we do not sell data or use it for advertising; and you can delete it at any time.</p>\n\n    <h3>2. What we collect</h3>\n    <ul class=\"list\">\n      <li><b>Registration details:</b> name, phone and email as submitted.</li>\n      <li><b>Conversation content:</b> your messages and the Agent's replies pass through our systems and are processed automatically to respond and operate the Service.</li>\n      <li><b>Usage and technical data:</b> task types, usage patterns (frequency, times, session length), feature usage, errors and performance, and technical identifiers for routing (such as your Telegram ID).</li>\n    </ul>\n    <p>We do not collect payment details, use advertising trackers, or buy data from third parties. Please avoid sharing especially sensitive information (medical, financial, biometric) unless needed for a task.</p>\n\n    <h3>3. How we use it</h3>\n    <ul class=\"list\">\n      <li><b>Operating the Service:</b> processing messages, maintaining context, providing support.</li>\n      <li><b>Improvement:</b> understanding task types and failure points — from usage data and aggregate statistics, not from reading personal content.</li>\n      <li><b>AI research and development:</b> a noncommercial use; we do not sell data, share it for advertising, or target you with marketing.</li>\n      <li><b>Safety and security:</b> preventing abuse and enforcing the Terms.</li>\n      <li><b>Communication:</b> messages about the pilot itself.</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <h3>4. Who accesses your information</h3>\n    <p>We do not read conversations as a routine practice; analysis and research rely on usage data and aggregate statistics. Your content is not published, sold or exposed to third parties outside the systems operating the Service. Access to raw content is technically restricted, and we access a specific chat only in limited cases: fixing a fault, a support request from you, a legal obligation, or investigating abuse or a security incident — and only to the extent needed.</p>\n\n    <h3>5. Sharing and processors</h3>\n    <p>We do not sell data or share it for advertising. Sharing is only with providers needed to operate the Service: Telegram (delivering messages under its policy), model providers (processing for the responses, under a use-restricting agreement), and hosting and infrastructure providers. We will disclose information if required by law or court order, or to protect rights in a dispute, and on a transfer of the activity to another entity (merger/acquisition) subject to this policy. Some processing occurs on servers outside Israel, in accordance with the Privacy Protection Regulations (Transfer of Data Abroad), 2001.</p>\n\n    <h3>6. Retention and deletion</h3>\n    <ul class=\"list\">\n      <li>We keep your data while you participate.</li>\n      <li>You can delete your chat and request deletion at any time (via the Agent or <a href=\"mailto:elia@bencnaan.net\">elia@bencnaan.net</a>). We complete deletion from active systems within 30 days, except minimal records required by law or needed for an open dispute.</li>\n      <li>Personal data from the pilot is deleted or anonymized within 90 days of its end, unless you asked to be kept informed of future versions.</li>\n      <li>Statistics that do not identify anyone may be retained and used after deletion.</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <h3>7. Your rights</h3>\n    <ul class=\"list\">\n      <li><b>Voluntary:</b> you have no legal duty to provide information; it depends on your consent. Without registration details we cannot include you — that is the only consequence.</li>\n      <li><b>Access and correction:</b> under the Israeli Privacy Protection Law, 1981, you may review your information and request correction or deletion of inaccurate data — at <a href=\"mailto:elia@bencnaan.net\">elia@bencnaan.net</a>.</li>\n      <li><b>Complaint:</b> you may contact the Israeli Privacy Protection Authority.</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <h3>8. Security</h3>\n    <p>We apply technical and organizational measures appropriate to this pilot (access controls, encryption in transit). No service is completely secure, so use judgment about what you share.</p>\n\n    <h3>9. Age</h3>\n    <p>The Service is for adults 18 and over. We do not knowingly collect information from minors; if you believe one has provided data, write to <a href=\"mailto:elia@bencnaan.net\">elia@bencnaan.net</a> and we will delete it.</p>\n\n    <h3>10. Changes to this policy</h3>\n    <p>We may update this policy from time to time. For a material change to how we handle your personal information we will give advance notice. The current version is always available where the pilot documents are published.</p>\n\n    <h3>11. Contact</h3>\n    <p>Data controller: NanoCo. For any privacy question, request or complaint: <a href=\"mailto:elia@bencnaan.net\">elia@bencnaan.net</a>.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <a class=\"back\" href=\"/\">← Back</a>\n</div>\n\n<script>\n  function setLang(l){\n    var html=document.documentElement;\n    html.lang=l; html.dir=(l==='he'?'rtl':'ltr');\n    document.getElementById('btnHe').classList.toggle('on', l==='he');\n    document.getElementById('btnEn').classList.toggle('on', l==='en');\n    try{ localStorage.setItem('lang', l); }catch(e){}\n  }\n  (function(){\n    var p=new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('lang');\n    var saved; try{ saved=localStorage.getItem('lang'); }catch(e){}\n    var l=(p==='en'||p==='he')?p:(saved==='en'?'en':'he');\n    if(l==='en') setLang('en');\n  })();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":136,"cache_read_input_tokens":106609,"output_tokens":14189,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"serv